{
"Version": "2012-10-17",
"Statement": [
{
"Effect": "Allow",
"Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
"Resource": [
"arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket",
"arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*"
]
}
]
}
Parts:
Effect — Allow or Deny.
Action — service:operation. Wildcards allowed (s3:Get*).
Resource — ARN(s) the actions apply to. * means "all resources".
Optional: Condition, Principal, NotAction, NotResource.

Write a JSON policy that allows the holder to list all S3 buckets and read (GetObject) from a single bucket named course-notes, but nothing else.
Solution
{
"Version": "2012-10-17",
"Statement": [
{ "Effect": "Allow", "Action": "s3:ListAllMyBuckets", "Resource": "*" },
{ "Effect": "Allow", "Action": "s3:ListBucket", "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::course-notes" },
{ "Effect": "Allow", "Action": "s3:GetObject", "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::course-notes/*" }
]
}
